Verified by building `canary` d64ebedd0 with this patch (together with the fixes from my other reports) and upgrading the vulnerable test instance in place. Typecheck passes for `packages/server` and `apps/dokploy`; the vitest suite shows the same 7 failures with and without the change.

After the fix, as member B: `schedule.one`, `deployment.allByType`, `readLogs`, `killProcess` and `removeDeployment` all return `FORBIDDEN`, and org A's job keeps running. As owner of org A: `readLogs`, `schedule.one` and `killProcess` work; a second `killProcess` on the finished deployment returns `BAD_REQUEST Deployment is not running`.

Not addressed: `deployment.allByType` with `type: "backup"` for web-server backups (no service attached) falls back to `checkPermission(ctx, { deployment: ["read"] })` only, which any member has.
